1
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:04,850
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:10,590
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,530 --> 00:00:14,520
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,430
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,500
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:16,510
Feel no shame about shape

7
00:01:16,590 --> 00:01:18,430
Weather changes their phrase

8
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:22,180
Even mother will show you another way

9
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:24,560
So put your glasses on

10
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:26,640
Nothing will be wrong

11
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:28,850
There's no blame. There's no fame

12
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:30,690
It's up to you

13
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:34,320
The first words should be found

14
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:37,950
Whatever holds you back

15
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:39,320
I...

16
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,450
...can...

17
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:42,620
I can get it off

18
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:43,620
Tell me what...

19
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:44,620
Tell me what...

20
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,460
Tell me what you want

21
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:47,540
I don't know why...

22
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:48,540
Don't know why...

23
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:50,540
Don't know why you're afraid

24
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:51,710
Tell me what...

25
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:52,670
Tell me what...

26
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,340
Tell me what you'd say

27
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,670
I don't know why...

28
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:56,760
Don't know why...

29
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:57,550
Too late...

30
00:01:57,630 --> 00:01:59,180
It's too late

31
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,100
Zodd the Immortal

32
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:33,630
Message!

33
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:39,800
We have successfully brought
the enemy castle under control!

34
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,180
And the castle's commander?

35
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:42,720
We have not yet reached him...

36
00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:46,430
The Raiders, under Guts's
command, are laying siege...

37
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:48,020
...to the castle's keep, but...

38
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:52,350
Due to the one immensely powerful
soldier who is with the enemy...

39
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:54,400
...we cannot clear a path!

40
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:55,860
Only one?

41
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:58,990
Cut off by one soldier?

42
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,860
What a pathetic commander!

43
00:03:07,790 --> 00:03:08,910
Zodd...

44
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,210
What?

45
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,370
What was that, Judeau?

46
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:17,550
It's something I heard about
before we joined the war effort.

47
00:03:17,550 --> 00:03:21,430
It's said Nosferatu Zodd sometimes
fights among the enemy lines...

48
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:23,300
Nosferatu...

49
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,600
Zodd the Immortal?

50
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:27,810
Zodd?

51
00:03:28,350 --> 00:03:29,600
Zodd the Immortal?

52
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:33,480
Who is he?

53
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:35,310
Haven't you heard of him, Pippin?

54
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:38,440
Zodd the Immortal...

55
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:42,150
He is well-known as a
legendary fighter among mercenaries.

56
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:47,580
They say he's taken the heads of
hundreds or even thousands in battle...

57
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:53,790
And that's not the only
reason why he is feared...

58
00:03:55,830 --> 00:04:01,550
Sometimes he returns to battle after
reportedly being killed in another one.

59
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:07,220
Believe it or not, he's been
around for nearly a hundred years...

60
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:09,310
...according to the accounts of his exploits.

61
00:04:10,470 --> 00:04:11,930
A hundred years?

62
00:04:12,430 --> 00:04:15,150
That is why he is called Zodd the Immortal.

63
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,940
Hey, give me a break!

64
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:21,320
You aren't going to take that
kind of fairy tale seriously, are you...

65
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:23,280
...Ricky boy?

66
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,360
But as a matter of fact...

67
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:28,120
...some mercenaries worship
Zodd as the God of Battle!

68
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:29,830
Okay, okay...

69
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:38,380
I don't like the look of the sky...

70
00:04:47,090 --> 00:04:48,510
Let go of me, Gaston!

71
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:50,060
No way, Commander!

72
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:52,640
Hey, you all gotta help
me stop the commander!

73
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,020
Y-You!

74
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:56,350
I won't let you go no matter what!

75
00:04:56,350 --> 00:04:59,020
We just can't let our commander go in alone!

76
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,520
Shut up! Don't touch me!

77
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,610
Just wait!

78
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,570
We should wait a little bit more!

79
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,280
Don't be an idiot!

80
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:09,240
It's been almost two hours since
I sent out fifty of my soldiers!

81
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:11,120
I can't leave them!

82
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:13,000
Then...

83
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,080
Please ask Captain Griffith for reinforcements!

84
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:16,960
Do it if you dare...

85
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,040
...but I'll kill you!

86
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:19,630
One soldier!

87
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:23,840
One soldier has nailed down
all five hundred of our raiders!

88
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:25,670
We cannot move forward like this!

89
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:28,720
This is completely humiliating!

90
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:30,600
C-Commander!

91
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,180
D-Dillos!

92
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:33,850
Commander Guts, it's Dillos!

93
00:05:33,850 --> 00:05:35,270
Dillos! It's Dillos!

94
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,480
Dillos, are you okay?

95
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,190
Commander!

96
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:40,940
Dillos...

97
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:43,980
C-Commander!

98
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,280
Hang on!

99
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:49,490
Zodd...

100
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,120
What?

101
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,530
What did you say, Dillos?

102
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:54,580
Zodd the...

103
00:05:55,370 --> 00:05:56,290
...Immortal!

104
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:01,840
Zodd?

105
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:05,590
So that rumor was true after all...

106
00:06:06,050 --> 00:06:08,260
Hey, we're in big trouble...

107
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:09,590
Commander...

108
00:06:20,810 --> 00:06:22,900
H-Hold on a minute, Commander!

109
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:23,610
Stay back!

110
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,190
Make sure no one follows me.

111
00:06:27,610 --> 00:06:29,110
I will settle this alone...

112
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,540
Commander...

113
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,170
What the hell...

114
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:45,710
What...

115
00:08:46,170 --> 00:08:47,920
What the hell is this?

116
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:53,420
You evaded my strike well, boy.

117
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:19,320
Amazing...

118
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,290
A monster...

119
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,250
I'll go take a look inside.

120
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:30,840
The rest of you, stay here and wait.

121
00:09:31,250 --> 00:09:32,960
B-But...

122
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:33,960
I'll go with you.

123
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:37,430
Don't worry, I will definitely bring Guts back.

124
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:39,680
Now move out!

125
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:40,640
Yes, sir!

126
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,940
During the last fifty years, no one...

127
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:52,110
...could defend against my moves like you can.

128
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:56,530
He is stronger than any
swordsman I have ever fought...

129
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:58,200
He is far stronger...

130
00:09:58,570 --> 00:09:59,870
He is the strongest...

131
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:04,410
No, that's not it,
his strength is more than human.

132
00:10:04,410 --> 00:10:05,540
What can I do?

133
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:07,290
I can't evade his strikes much longer.

134
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:11,670
I've only been able to defend myself
so far because of my blade's size.

135
00:10:12,090 --> 00:10:15,090
Just one of his strikes
would easily cleave a normal sword.

136
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:19,840
So the strength of our
weapons is at least equal...

137
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:25,640
I see...

138
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:28,640
You intend to gamble
your life on a single strike...

139
00:10:31,310 --> 00:10:34,690
It looks like you are going
to try for one final opportunity...

140
00:10:34,690 --> 00:10:37,320
...by relying on the length of your blade.

141
00:10:37,690 --> 00:10:39,400
But your idea is flawed.

142
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:42,620
Your brains will be scattered across
this room before you reach me.

143
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,200
Sounds like fun!

144
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,990
I accept your challenge!

145
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:56,300
You brat!

146
00:11:09,270 --> 00:11:11,400
This is the first time...

147
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,610
That my body...

148
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:19,150
...has been so deeply stabbed...

149
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:22,280
...with a sword of...

150
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:24,240
...a human like you...

151
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:34,710
Throughout my three hundred
years of slaughtering, you are the first...

152
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:37,840
...who has stabbed me like this.

153
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:20,710
I'm getting excited!

154
00:12:21,170 --> 00:12:25,680
You've made my blood boil
as it has not in many years.

155
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:30,310
To feel like this once again...

156
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:33,560
To meet an opponent like you...

157
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:38,060
For the past three hundred
years, I have lived for this!

158
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,490
Now, fight with me!

159
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:45,860
You must not let me down!

160
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,170
It's impossible...

161
00:12:58,040 --> 00:13:00,710
There's no way that a monster...

162
00:13:01,630 --> 00:13:04,010
...like this could really exist!

163
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:38,920
What's wrong?

164
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:41,340
Are you giving up?

165
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:47,470
Is this the limit to your strength?

166
00:13:47,470 --> 00:13:49,430
Is there no more?

167
00:13:50,050 --> 00:13:54,560
I suppose I can say you have
done very well, for a human...

168
00:13:55,230 --> 00:13:59,060
...but if you cannot fight
anymore, I will tear your body...

169
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:00,650
...into pieces!

170
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:25,260
Griffith...

171
00:14:26,630 --> 00:14:28,930
H-Hey, what the hell is that?

172
00:14:29,590 --> 00:14:32,510
Is he Nosferatu Zodd?

173
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:34,140
Keep your guard up!

174
00:14:34,470 --> 00:14:35,180
Another volley!

175
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,230
Shoot!

176
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,060
Did we get him?

177
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:54,280
You shall not be forgiven!

178
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:01,330
I will not forgive anyone who gets in the way...

179
00:15:01,330 --> 00:15:03,420
...of our battle!

180
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,300
No hope!

181
00:15:09,170 --> 00:15:11,260
R-Run away!

182
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:23,610
What's wrong with Griffith?

183
00:15:23,610 --> 00:15:26,150
Nobody's returned yet!

184
00:15:26,150 --> 00:15:27,230
I wonder...

185
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:32,450
...if Zodd already killed off the
commander and Sir Griffith as well...

186
00:15:33,370 --> 00:15:35,370
Don't talk nonsense, Gaston!

187
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:38,410
It's not possible that those two were killed!

188
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:39,960
But it's taking so long...

189
00:15:40,370 --> 00:15:41,750
What should we do, Casca?

190
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,210
Keep on waiting here.

191
00:15:44,210 --> 00:15:46,040
Aren't you worried about them?

192
00:15:47,050 --> 00:15:49,090
Griffith ordered us to wait.

193
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:05,730
Monster!

194
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,490
All of you, retreat immediately.

195
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:18,280
C-Captain...

196
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,540
Go right away!

197
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:20,580
Captain!

198
00:16:27,210 --> 00:16:28,170
Are you all right?

199
00:16:29,670 --> 00:16:31,090
You're such a fool...

200
00:16:31,090 --> 00:16:32,010
Why did you come?

201
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:36,760
You can complain all you like after we escape.

202
00:16:37,010 --> 00:16:38,050
Why?

203
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:41,060
Why have things come to this?

204
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,860
Where are you going?

205
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:50,780
I still can hear your heartbeat...

206
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,610
Fight on!

207
00:16:54,610 --> 00:16:58,320
You must fight with me
until your body is torn apart!

208
00:17:01,410 --> 00:17:02,250
Can you move?

209
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:04,160
We'll be killed if I don't.

210
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:08,290
Good, you attack from the right!

211
00:17:09,710 --> 00:17:10,460
Let's go!

212
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:35,700
Guts!

213
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:37,320
We'll sprint past him towards the exit!

214
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:38,030
Right!

215
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:46,370
Griffith!

216
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:52,380
What a day...

217
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,550
What a day this has been!

218
00:17:56,010 --> 00:17:57,720
It's remarkable...

219
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:02,680
I've encountered two men who are
able to inflict wounds on my body...

220
00:18:08,230 --> 00:18:12,900
And to think I'll lose them
both at the same time...

221
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:22,740
Griffith...

222
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:26,000
First, I'll take care of this one.

223
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:31,380
T-This is...

224
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:34,590
The Egg of the King!

225
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:38,260
T-That cannot be...

226
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:43,970
A boy like him possesses
the Crimson Behelit of the God Hand...

227
00:18:56,690 --> 00:18:58,070
I see!

228
00:18:58,070 --> 00:19:00,030
So that's the ploy...

229
00:19:08,450 --> 00:19:10,370
W-What's that?

230
00:19:10,370 --> 00:19:11,040
Commander...

231
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,420
Griffith...

232
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:16,590
Casca!

233
00:19:17,210 --> 00:19:18,920
All right, everyone follow her!

234
00:19:22,090 --> 00:19:23,140
Boy...

235
00:19:23,930 --> 00:19:26,720
...we'll suspend our duel for the time being.

236
00:19:27,470 --> 00:19:32,850
Unfortunately, I doubt I will
have another chance to fight you.

237
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,520
I will give you some advice...

238
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:38,110
Or rather, I will foretell your doom...

239
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:46,740
If you and this man truly regard each
other as friends, be mindful of this...

240
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:51,710
When this man's ambition crumbles...

241
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:59,170
...you will be destined to face your death!

242
00:19:59,170 --> 00:20:02,050
A death you can never escape!

243
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:15,480
W-What is that?

244
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,190
A-A demon?

245
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:29,790
Death?

246
00:20:30,830 --> 00:20:32,660
Am I going to die?

247
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:46,510
Griffith!

248
00:20:46,970 --> 00:20:48,470
Are both of you all right?

249
00:20:52,310 --> 00:20:53,940
Guts, are you okay?

250
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:54,850
Yeah...

251
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:58,150
Only the two of you could survive this...

252
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,110
It's terrible...

253
00:21:05,110 --> 00:21:06,910
What really happened here?

254
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:08,780
Griffith!

255
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,620
Hold on!

256
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:11,620
Griffith!

257
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:13,540
Griffith!

258
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,210
Griffith!

259
00:21:24,510 --> 00:21:25,840
Don't touch him!

260
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:28,430
Don't touch Griffith!

261
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:33,180
It's your fault...

262
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:36,060
You put Griffith in danger
and almost got him killed...

263
00:21:37,190 --> 00:21:38,730
It's all your fault!

264
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

265
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

266
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

267
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

268
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

269
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

270
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

271
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

272
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

273
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

274
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

